---
title: Quinoa Salad with Roasted Vegetables
servings: 4
cuisine: mediterranean
main_protein: none
prep_time: "25 minutes"
cook_time: "35 minutes"
tags:
  - side
prep:
  - Preheat oven to 425°F and line two rimmed baking sheets with parchment
  - Dice the eggplant, zucchini and yellow squash
  - Rinse 0.5 cup quinoa
  - Press or mince 1 garlic clove and halve the grape tomatoes
  - Chop basil and mint
---

Preheat #oven{} to 425 degrees Fahrenheit with racks in the upper and lower thirds of the oven. Line two large, #rimmed baking sheets{} with parchment paper.

Divide the @eggplant{1}, diced, @zucchini{1}, diced, and @yellow squash{1}, diced, between the two baking sheets. Drizzle each baking sheet with 1 tablespoon of the @olive oil{4%tbsp} (divided; the rest goes in the dressing) and toss. (Add a little more if necessary; you want enough to lightly coat the vegetables.) Sprinkle each pan with ¼ teaspoon @salt{} and 5 twists of @black pepper{}. Roast until the veggies are softened and browning along the edges, about ~{25%minutes}. Set the roasted vegetables aside to cool.

To cook the quinoa, combine the @quinoa{0.5%cup}, rinsed, with @water{1%cup} in a #small saucepan{}. Bring to boil over medium-high heat, then cover and reduce heat to low. Simmer until the water is absorbed, about ~{15%minutes}, then remove from heat and let the quinoa steam with the lid on for ~{5%minutes}. Remove lid, fluff the quinoa with a fork and set aside.

To toast the @sliced almonds{0.25%cup} (or pine nuts), cook them in a #small skillet{} over medium heat, stirring frequently, until they're turning lightly golden and fragrant, about ~{4%minutes}. Be sure to keep an eye on them so they don't burn. Transfer them to a bowl to cool.

In a #large serving bowl{}, whisk together 2 tablespoons of the @lemon juice{2%tbsp} and @garlic{1%clove}, pressed or minced. Slowly pour in the remaining 2 tablespoons of olive oil while whisking constantly. Add the @grape tomatoes{1%cup}, halved, quinoa, @fresh basil{0.67%oz}, chopped, @fresh mint{0.67%oz}, chopped, roasted vegetables and nuts, and gently stir to combine. Season generously with salt (I add another ¼ teaspoon or more), pepper and maybe another squeeze of lemon, to taste. Stir in the @feta{0.5%cup}, crumbled, if you'd like. Serve at room temperature. Store in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 5 days.

-- Make it dairy free/vegan: Skip the feta and add some sliced, pitted Kalamata olives to make up for feta's salty punch.
